{
  "dom_id": "step-q39056",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\le 2,\\,2\\le x+y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nBy performing the change of variables\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,v=x+y,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nthe triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x+y)\\operatorname{sinh}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dV\n$$\n\ncan be written in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w$ as",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
